#
# Conformance case: holonic/holonic-level
# AC: logic:holonicLevel coherence + its NON-CONFLATION with the instantiation
#     tower (logic:orderedType / logic:instanceOf) (issue #708, C5).
#
# A holon's logic:holonicLevel (mereological compositional depth) is READ OFF its
# logic:HolonicPosition — the canonical relational construct of which logic:Holon
# and a level are lossy projections. The level itself is a literal and the
# foundation chase is all-IRI, so coherence is keyed on the IRI-valued canonical
# construct: a profiled holon must occupy a logic:HolonicPosition (some position
# reifier with logic:positionEntity back to the holon). Without one there is no
# path along which a depth can be measured, so the level is incoherent.
#
# logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence is PROFILE-SCOPED, exactly like
# logic:WeakSupplementation: only a holon declared under a logic:MereologyProfile
# (via logic:underMereologyProfile) is charged; a holon outside any profile is
# never charged (#775 profile-relativity).
#
# Three strict-parthood chains exercise the trichotomy. Every profiled holon is
# given TWO disjoint proper parts so weak supplementation is satisfied and the case
# isolates level coherence (no logic:WeakSupplementation noise):
#
#   * ex:Bracket — profiled holon (Bolt1, Bolt2 ⊏ Bracket ⊏ Assembly) that occupies
#     a logic:HolonicPosition (ex:posBracket positionEntity ex:Bracket) → COHERENT,
#     no violation.
#   * ex:Gearbox — profiled holon (Gear1, Gear2 ⊏ Gearbox ⊏ Drivetrain) that is high
#     in the INSTANTIATION tower (logic:instanceOf ex:GearboxKind) but occupies NO
#     logic:HolonicPosition → fires logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence. Instantiation
#     order does NOT supply a holonic position — the non-conflation guarantee.
#   * ex:Sprite — UNPROFILED holon (Pixel1, Pixel2 ⊏ Sprite ⊏ Scene) with no position
#     → never charged (profile-relativity).
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the parthood edges,
# the profile membership, the position reifier, and the instantiation edge are
# duplicated there in the named world ex:schema; these are the program axioms.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/holonic/holonic-level/> .

ex:MP a logic:MereologyProfile .

# Chain 1 — coherent profiled holon (occupies a logic:HolonicPosition).
ex:Bolt1   logic:properPartOf         ex:Bracket .
ex:Bolt2   logic:properPartOf         ex:Bracket .
ex:Bracket logic:properPartOf         ex:Assembly .
ex:Bracket logic:underMereologyProfile ex:MP .
ex:posBracket logic:positionEntity    ex:Bracket .

# Chain 2 — profiled holon in the instantiation tower but with NO position
# (non-conflation: instantiation order does not supply a holonic position → fires).
ex:Gear1   logic:properPartOf         ex:Gearbox .
ex:Gear2   logic:properPartOf         ex:Gearbox .
ex:Gearbox logic:properPartOf         ex:Drivetrain .
ex:Gearbox logic:underMereologyProfile ex:MP .
ex:Gearbox logic:instanceOf           ex:GearboxKind .

# Chain 3 — unprofiled holon, no position (profile-relativity: never charged).
ex:Pixel1  logic:properPartOf         ex:Sprite .
ex:Pixel2  logic:properPartOf         ex:Sprite .
ex:Sprite  logic:properPartOf         ex:Scene .
